    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1592">

                <pb facs="1170" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.5212/32.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 25, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: In the note which I
                    addressed to you on February 6 last, on the subject of the attempt to arrest Sr.
                    Angel del Caso by order of General Carranza, I stated inadvertently that Sr. del
                    Caso was the Confidential Agent of the Spanish Government to <pb facs="1171"
                        n="1055" xml:id="pg1055"/> General Villa; but I have subsequently been
                    informed by my colleague the Spanish Minister to Mexico, that Sr. del Caso’s
                    appointment of Confidential Agent of the Spanish Government was to the President
                    elected by the Convention of Aguascalientes.</p>
                <p>Please take note of this information and believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
